      "bio.transition.title": "From Winger to Right Back",
      "bio.transition.p1": "In late 2023, Monaco coach Adi Hütter began using Diatta at right back, and he later featured as a right wing-back in a 3-4-3 under Sébastien Pocognoli. The switch took time, but his professionalism and athleticism helped him master the defensive side of the game.",
      "bio.transition.p2": "The transformation paid off: in 2025/26 he became a regular on Monaco's right side, and for Senegal he locked down the right-back spot, helping the Lions win the 2026 AFCON and play at the 2026 World Cup. The former flying winger is now a reliable right-sided anchor.",
      "bio.monaco.title": "At Monaco",
      "bio.monaco.p": "In January 2021, Diatta joined AS Monaco from Club Brugge for a reported €20m fee, signing a deal until 2025. After a serious injury in 2021, he worked his way back and returned to action in 2022. From late 2023, coach Adi Hütter began converting him into a right back / right wing-back, and his two-way performances made him a regular on Monaco's right side again.",

